+## A1 SQL geometry correction (implementation; acceptance pending)
+
+The first actual combined A1 preflight failed in the Go reference at `sql-scroll-500-120x40-dark`: `resize-large` repainted 140×45, but the closed-drawer footer predicate never qualified. The 62s session timeout prevented `resize-original` and the Rust capture. The resulting missing resize event then raised `captured resize sequence differs from declared script`. The original report, sessions, raw bytes and independent diagnosis remain unchanged; see `docs/phase7-review-a1-functional-failure-opus-r1.md`.
+
+The collector now follows the default **open** columns drawer without changing any case, action, key, count, seed, wait definition or fixture. Go `pkg/model/query.go` initializes `columnsDrawerOpen: true` and its `View` computes `sidebarW=34` (`sqlControlsMinWidth`), adding 3 at W≥140, then `editorW=max(30,W−sidebarW−1)`. With full-height controls, `resultsW=editorW`. Rust `src/tui/sql.rs` initializes the same state and mirrors those calculations. Thus the footer on zero-based row H−6 must end exclusively at `resultsW−3`: 82 at 120×40 and 99 at 140×45. On both that row and selected-marker row 16, readiness requires results borders at 0/resultsW−1, the blank one-column gap at resultsW, and sidebar borders at resultsW+1/W−1. The marker must lie inside the results pane. Existing actual-dimensions, post-action output, changed-frame, corner and 80ms styled stability checks remain in force.
+
+Functional preflight records per-role `capture_failure` and `termination` immediately after `sample` returns, before artifact/binding validation. They describe the returned capture only; they grant no validity. The existing binding exception still aborts before subsequent validation/comparison or the candidate role, leaves the report invalid, and is retained alongside the original timeout. There is no catch-and-continue or subset admission.
+
+`docs/evidence/phase7/a1-geometry-retained-go.json.gz` contains hash-bound 120×40 `return-first` and 140×45 final Go frames, their original raw stream, exact resize offset, source identities and the original compiled-predicate control. Pure tests reconstruct both full styled frames exactly, reject wrong footer columns/rows, closed-drawer full-width geometry, misplaced markers, broken pane/sidebar/outer borders and gaps, and partial old frames during grow/shrink. The original predicate rejects both actual targets while accepting its synthetic closed-drawer control. Refeeding the retained 120×40 bytes after a shrink is a pure emulator control, not an observed native shrink. A mock timeout plus the real downstream binding exception proves that both diagnostics survive and the candidate remains unrun; compiled removal of the new reporting assignments removes only those diagnostics.
+
+PromQL `dense_table_geometry` is unchanged. Source inference: Go `pkg/model/promql.go` computes `resultsInnerW=m.width−4` and renders the results pane with `m.width`; Rust `src/tui/promql.rs` computes its inner width from `self.width` and passes `self.width` to `results_pane`. Its results span the full terminal width, so SQL's drawer correction does not transfer. No actual PromQL capture or successful matching preflight is established here. Fresh independent review and root's actual Go/Rust preflight remain required; this implementation is not acceptance or a performance claim.
